[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Sicilian Defense: Alapin Variation"]
[Variation "Alapin Variation, Barmen Defense, Central Exchange"]
[ECO "B22"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "pin"]
[Themes "tempo-gain,d4-pawn-centre"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "4...Nc6"]
[Start "d5-main-line 4.d4"]

4... Nc6 5. Nf3 Bg4 ( 5... Nf6 { The same position as 4...Nf6 5.Nf3 Nc6, where 6.Be3 guards d4. } ) ( 5... e6 { The same position as 2...e6 3.d4 d5 4.exd5 Qxd5 5.Nf3 Nc6, where 6.Be3 guards d4. } ) 6. Be2 { Answers the pin by guarding the knight with the bishop. If Black takes on f3, White recaptures and the bishop pair is worth more than the pawn structure. } 6... cxd4 7. cxd4 e6 8. Nc3 { Now that the c-pawn has gone, the knight comes out with tempo on the queen. [%cal Gc3d5] } 8... Qa5 ( 8... Bb4 9. O-O { Castles before anything else: the pin on the knight is not dangerous, and if Black takes on c3, bxc3 guards d4 with a pawn again. } ) ( 8... Qd8 9. h3 { Asks the bishop to decide. If it takes on f3, White gets the two bishops and the bishop on f3 eyes b7. } ) ( 8... Qd7 9. O-O ) 9. O-O Nf6 10. h3 Bxf3 11. Bxf3 Rd8 12. Be3 *
